  // and processes to completion before the outer notification continues."
  // We wrap the dispatch logic to ensure the loop continues correctly.
  // However, the standard Redux pattern handles this by the fact that 
  // dispatching sets isDispatching=true, and the loop is already running.
  // To strictly follow "processes to completion before the outer notification continues",
  // we use a recursive-friendly approach or simply rely on the synchronous nature.

  // Re-implementing dispatch to handle nested dispatches correctly:
  function dispatch(action) {
    if (isDispatching) {
      throw new Error('Reducers may not dispatch actions.');
    }

    isDispatching = true;
    try {
      state = reducer(state, action);
